WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.660
The first film placed fossil whales in time.

2
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:08.400
If that history is right, what should we find inside living whales and their DNA?

3
00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:14.013
Keep one branching tree in view.

4
00:00:15.273 --> 00:00:20.713
A common ancestor is an ancestral population from which later species descended.

5
00:00:22.173 --> 00:00:24.353
Branches split; they do not form a ladder.

6
00:00:25.913 --> 00:00:27.153
Living species sit at the tips.

7
00:00:28.217 --> 00:00:30.697
DNA passes from parents to offspring.

8
00:00:32.217 --> 00:00:34.817
Small copied changes can travel down a branch.

9
00:00:36.217 --> 00:00:39.677
Nearby branches have had less time to collect different changes.

10
00:00:41.117 --> 00:00:44.477
Matching DNA stretches are therefore usually more similar.

11
00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:50.707
Suppose an insertion spread through the ancestral population of whales and hippos

12
00:00:50.707 --> 00:00:53.267
before they split, and was never lost.

13
00:00:54.627 --> 00:00:56.407
Where should matching markers appear today?

14
00:00:57.767 --> 00:01:00.407
Choose whale and hippo, whale and fish, or all three.

15
00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:09.290
The matching markers should reach whales and hippos.

16
00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:14.410
Researchers found shared insertions at the same spots in the genome.

17
00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:19.570
That pattern groups whales with hippos among even-toed hoofed mammals.

18
00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.340
That grouping does not mean hippos became whales.

19
00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.960
Both living groups occupy separate tips.

20
00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:32.120
They share an earlier population, then each branch continued changing.

21
00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.700
Relatives are not automatically ancestors.

22
00:01:36.933 --> 00:01:39.493
Anatomy tests the tree another way.

23
00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:44.333
Homologous structures come from one structure in a common ancestor.

24
00:01:45.793 --> 00:01:50.793
A whale flipper, a human arm and a bat wing hold the same set of bones, arranged

25
00:01:50.793 --> 00:01:51.793
differently.

26
00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:56.707
Living whales also carry small hip bones that support no legs.

27
00:01:58.007 --> 00:02:03.007
They are vestigial: reduced parts that have lost all or most of the job they did in

28
00:02:03.007 --> 00:02:06.667
ancestors. Vestigial does not mean useless.

29
00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:10.847
In males, these bones anchor muscles used in mating.

30
00:02:11.967 --> 00:02:14.187
Development supplies a fourth test.

31
00:02:15.447 --> 00:02:18.187
A spotted dolphin embryo begins hind-limb buds.

32
00:02:19.447 --> 00:02:22.967
The signals that keep a limb growing switch off early or never appear.

33
00:02:24.207 --> 00:02:25.667
The buds stop and break down.

34
00:02:26.867 --> 00:02:29.227
The embryo is not replaying its ancestors.

35
00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.100
Now bring the lanes together.

36
00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:35.300
Gold fossils show change through time.

37
00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:39.200
Blue DNA places whales on a mammal branch.

38
00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:44.300
Green anatomy and teal development preserve inherited patterns.

39
00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:47.280
Different methods fit one history.

40
00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.740
Agreement is not certainty, and each test has limits.

41
00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:56.320
Fossil sequences do not identify direct parents.

42
00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:00.220
Similarity matters only for comparable DNA.

43
00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:04.320
A useful structure can still record ancestry.

44
00:03:05.533 --> 00:03:10.653
A scientific theory is a tested explanation that connects many observations.

45
00:03:12.153 --> 00:03:16.753
Evolution predicts related patterns before each evidence lane is opened.

46
00:03:18.173 --> 00:03:22.853
Confidence grows when those patterns appear across methods, not because any label

47
00:03:22.853 --> 00:03:23.853
says proof.

48
00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:27.207
Each method could have pointed to another history.

49
00:03:28.607 --> 00:03:31.087
Instead, their patterns agree within their limits.

50
00:03:32.827 --> 00:03:37.147
Independent evidence that agrees strengthens an explanation of common descent.
